{
  "abstract": "For OEIS A212334, given for n >= 1 by a(n) = sum over 0 <= k < n of C(n,k) C(n-1,k) C(n+k-1,k)^2, with a(0) = 1, a Lean 4 and Mathlib proof that a(p) is congruent to 1 modulo p^5 for every prime p >= 5. Peter Bala recorded this congruence as an observation in the OEIS entry in December 2021. An earlier informal proof of the same congruence is public, and no priority is claimed. The binomial sum is taken as the definition; its agreement with the word-counting definition in OEIS, and the higher prime-power congruences conjectured in the same entry, are not formalized.",
